Dear Robert,

As I transition out of the role, I am handing over the integrity files for the ATU-100. Please review QSCP-RCA-2007-002 regarding the 2-RV-102 elbow leak caused by localized acid gas condensation. The investigation identified that CMLs were previously restricted to straight runs, which missed the thinning at the fitting.

In response, we issued QSCP-IP-ATU100 Rev 1 to update the piping inspection plan. We have added 20 fitting CMLs for a total of 138 points and set the regenerator overhead circuit to a 3-year interval. The failed elbow has been replaced and the new monitoring locations are now active in the database.

Best regards,  Gordon Lisle Unit Engineer ATU-100, P.Eng. To: Robert Hendricks

Gordon Lisle, Unit Engineer ATU-100, P.Eng., QSCP Hamilton Inspection Department